{
  "$comment": "EXP-1602: eUI Motion validation (apps/desktop/crates/eui-motion/src/validate.rs; the limits are catalog/limits.json › motion): what a Motion source is refused for (`errors`) and what it loads with as notes (`warnings`). AUTO-GENERATED expected codes: `UPDATE_MOTION_FIXTURES=1 cargo test -p eui-motion --test validate` (inputs kept). Each case: `id`, `covers`, ONE input, then `errors` and `warnings`: the issue CODES, compared as sorted multisets (paths and messages are informative, not part of the contract). Inputs: `lottie` = a document, serialised as compact JSON (no whitespace, keys in the order given); `source` = the raw UTF-8 bytes (parse errors); `build` = a generated input: `build.lottie` (compact JSON as above, integers and plain strings only, so every language serialises it byte-identically) with `repeatShapes: {count, shape}` = the first layer's `shapes` set to `count` copies of `shape`, then `padToBytes: N` = ASCII spaces appended until the source is exactly N bytes (trailing whitespace is valid JSON). Codes: `parse` (not JSON), `timing` (needs fr > 0 and op > ip), `limit-bytes` (source > maxBytes, checked first: nothing else runs), `limit-duration` ((op − ip) / fr > maxSeconds), `limit-shapes` (more than maxShapes shape items: every object with a string `ty` inside a layer's `shapes` or a group's `it`), `expression` (an animated property, an object with `k`, carrying an `x` STRING; one per property; ease handles' `x` arrays are not expressions); warnings are the engine's notes on features it renders approximately or skips.",
